WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.740
- So for the majority of my life,

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.130
I struggled to go to the gym consistently,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:07.120
even though the gym has
always been a part of my life

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.350
to some degree.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.650
I grew up playing hockey

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.010
and all my brothers played
hockey and went to the gym.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.940
So going to the gym was
always the right thing to do.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.350
But I could never stay consistent.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.530
Even into university,

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.760
sometimes I'd go two
weeks straight at the gym

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:20.950
and then take a month off.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.510
I'd try to get into a
groove and hype myself up,

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.700
and I really wanted to look like Thor.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.890
And then I lost my hair.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.000
The whole point of this
story is to let you know

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.480
that if you relate to this,

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.400
I've been in that exact same place.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.840
But I've managed in recent years

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.640
to develop a tremendous
consistency at the gym.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.230
And it takes me a lot
less effort to get there

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.880
than it previously ever has.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.440
And I can credit this a lot

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.740
to a particular mindset I've adopted

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.340
when it comes to doing things

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.400
that I find difficult or boring,

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.540
and sort of tricking my brain
into liking these things.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.320
I've also been able to apply this strategy

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.960
to other areas of my life.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.890
Most specifically to reading
books and editing videos.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.660
Essentially what I did is I
stopped generating motivation

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.370
by thinking about an end goal,

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.160
and instead I learned
to enjoy the process.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.810
So first of all, what's wrong
with visualizing an end goal?

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:15.280
Why not use this image of this beach body

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.410
or a Greek god physique
as motivation to work out?

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.720
Well, the main problem
you'll face is the fact

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:24.410
that there is a huge disparity
between what it feels like

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:27.000
to fantasize about this Greek god physique

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.390
and what it feels like to actually be

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:31.200
at the gym pushing heavy weights.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.100
They're are completely
different sensation.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.630
Fantasizing about having an
awesome body feels awesome.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.270
It puts you in this sort of La La Land

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.140
where you're just walking around

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.210
as this imaginary version of yourself.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.430
Actually going to the gym,
it's strenuous, it's sweaty.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:47.960
And it's often really boring,

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.120
especially if you're doing
cardio on a treadmill.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.320
It's the most boring thing

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.750
I've ever encountered in my life.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:53.870
That's the first problem.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.440
The second problem that you face

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.380
when you try to generate your motivation

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.700
from this ideal image of yourself

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.040
is that it will always be a moving target.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.910
No matter how much you fantasize

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.730
about this perfect version of yourself,

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.000
you will never feel like you have arrived.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.580
And even if you were to
hypothetically arrive at this goal,

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.020
there's something called entropy.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.250
Stagnation breeds destruction.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.830
If you just sit on your winnings,

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.200
everything will fall apart.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.670
You need to keep moving.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.660
You have to love the daily discipline

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.710
of going to battle every single day

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.460
and finding pleasure and
fulfillment in the thing,

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.690
in the present moment for its own sake.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.730
If you're able to do this,
then that's the happy place.

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:34.730
The thing itself will
generate its own motivation

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:35.670
as you do it.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.500
And you can become fully immersed

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.830
in the activity you're doing.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:41.190
So am I saying it's bad
to have goals in general?

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.023
Not at all.

00:02:42.023 --> 00:02:44.100
Goals are really good
for creating direction.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.270
Having an ideal is sort
of like having a compass.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.170
It's leading you in the right direction.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.430
You should take a glance
at it for reference,

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.130
but in the day-to-day struggle
of actually doing the thing,

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.620
it's not what you should be focusing on.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.310
So now that we know why
it's kind of unhelpful

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:00.120
to always think about this end goal,

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.240
now you're probably thinking,

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.720
how do I learn to enjoy and
embrace difficult things

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.060
and have it be an
integrated part of my life?

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.160
So there are two things that
really helped me do that.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.320
Number one is more of a mindset shift

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.620
and it's more inner work.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:17.530
And number two is more of a
practical, strategic thing

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.730
that you do to yourself.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:22.750
So number one is to operate
from an abundance mindset

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.550
rather than a scarcity mindset.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.610
When you think to yourself,
"I need to go get jacked,"

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:29.270
do you think that's an abundance mindset

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.900
or a scarcity mindset?

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:31.733
- [Child] Ready?

00:03:31.733 --> 00:03:32.566
Begin.

00:03:32.566 --> 00:03:34.740
(whimsical music)

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.730
- That is a scarcity mindset

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.640
because you need to go get something.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.020
And that applies that you
don't already have it.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.380
When you say I need to go to the gym

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.010
because I need to go get jacked,

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.770
you're subconsciously saying to yourself

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.470
that's because I'm not jacked yet.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.680
Which also implies to yourself
that you're not jacked.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.800
And as I've mentioned in previous videos,

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.310
human beings have an innate sense

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:58.240
of wanting to stay
intellectually consistent.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.630
Whatever you think your identity is,

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.280
you will operate accordingly.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.550
So if you are constantly telling yourself

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:07.610
that you are not jacked,
what do not jacked people do?

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:08.660
They don't go to the gym.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:09.830
When you look at it that way,

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.810
going to the gym will always be something

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.110
that's outside of yourself.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:15.430
It's something that's unnatural for you.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:17.740
Why would you go to the
gym if you're not jacked?

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.290
So am I saying you should
do some woo-woo thing

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:23.000
and pretend that you're
jacked all of a sudden?

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.690
Like force yourself to know

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:28.470
that you are in fact a giant beast?

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.810
That's not what I'm saying
because that's not true.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:32.670
Instead, try reminding yourself

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.440
that the reason why you
want to go to the gym

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.430
is because you're an active person,

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.810
and going to the gym is something
that is important to you.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:40.310
Your health is important to you.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:42.130
So since you're an active person,

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.260
going to the gym is just something you do.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.490
That gets rid of a ton of
mental resistance in the way

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:48.840
of actually going to the gym.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.260
You can use this exact same
method for reading books.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:53.860
If you're constantly telling yourself,

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.060
oh, I have to go read
books to get smarter.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.060
Oh, I have to go read a book now.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.130
Obviously you're not
gonna have a good time

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:00.963
while you're doing it.

00:05:00.963 --> 00:05:03.670
But if you identify as somebody
who enjoys reading books,

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.060
it's something that you like doing,

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:06.460
it's just a part of who you are,

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:07.510
then you're way more likely

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:09.310
to actually follow through with doing it.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:11.490
And if you think this is
just some woo-woo crap,

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.580
this is how some of
the greatest musicians,

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.660
athletes, and performers operate.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.240
Take John Mayer for example.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.500
I was just watching one of
his Instagram live videos

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.690
where he was jamming
out to blues backtracks

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.280
and he was having the time of his life.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.370
And he said on the actual livestream.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.010
- Nothing's more fun in this lifetime

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.010
going out to dinner and coming home

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.420
and picking up a guitar
and just practicing.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.253
Just play.

00:05:33.253 --> 00:05:34.230
I don't even call it practicing.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:36.660
- Because even the word practice implies

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.530
that you're only doing it to
achieve some sort of outcome.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:40.750
But if you're playing,

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.350
you're just enjoying it for what it is.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.280
- So when I'm playing for you,

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.420
I'm like, I'm kind of
doing what I do at home

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.220
which is repeat the same
stuff over and over again

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:48.320
'cause it feels really.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.710
- This next tip is a
little bit more practical

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:52.690
and a little less theoretical.

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:55.330
And that is to utilize habit-bunching.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.240
And that is when you pair
an already existing habit

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.910
that you are used to doing

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:01.840
with one that you're trying to work on.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.220
So for instance, I'm a sucker
for a great cup of coffee.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:08.140
I have one in the morning and
one in the early afternoon.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.890
I really enjoy the taste of coffee

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.380
and I look forward to
it every single time.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:13.890
Do I have an addiction?

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.870
Yes, but I can leverage
this filthy habit of mine

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:18.550
into working on another habit.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:21.880
A great one to pair with a
coffee addiction is reading.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.620
And that's exactly how I
started reading more books.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.920
Every single morning
next to my coffee maker,

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:29.780
I placed the book that I
wanted to read next to it

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.060
so that when I made my coffee,

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.630
I knew to pick up the book

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:34.600
and I could only drink the coffee

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:37.720
if I was reading the book the
entire time I was drinking it.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:38.553
Done.

00:06:38.553 --> 00:06:39.550
And the crazy thing about this

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.880
is eventually you just start
getting used to reading

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.510
whether you have coffee or not.

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:46.430
The action of opening
up a book and reading

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:47.960
becomes a lot more natural.

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:50.050
But it'll become something
very pleasant to you.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.830
That's so much better than reading

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:54.040
for the end goal of becoming smarter.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.440
What is getting smarter even feel like?

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.700
It doesn't feel like anything.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:58.890
It's not like in "The Matrix"

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.060
where they download kung fu onto Neo,

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.610
all of a sudden you just feel it.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.490
Habit-bunching also works really well

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.520
when you're trying to develop a gym habit.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:07.470
If you have an album

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:10.670
that you are currently in
the habit of listening to,

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:12.370
and you crave the sound

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:15.990
of Post Malone's beautiful,
sweet, silky melodies,

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.360
then you should leverage that.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.260
Allow yourself to listen to Post Malone,

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:21.870
but only when you're at the gym.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.300
This is one of the main ways I started

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.030
to become consistent at the gym.

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:29.580
I had this Migos album that
would pump me up so much.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.890
Even though I'm looking back on it now,

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:34.270
it's not even good music at all.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:36.700
And just like drinking coffee and reading,

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:38.830
once you start using habit-bunching

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:41.550
to develop a positive association

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:43.290
with the habit you're trying to work on,

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:46.160
then your entire mindset
towards that thing shifts.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.650
Pretty soon you will just
like going to the gym

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.360
because of the way it makes you feel.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:52.470
And realize that it's less about the music

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.170
that's actually making you feel so good,

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:55.810
and it's more about the endorphins

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:58.000
of pushing heavy weight
and getting stronger.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:58.990
So to summarize,

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.970
stop generating your motivation
on a day-to-day basis

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:04.520
by fantasizing about some sort of end goal

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.180
that you're never going to arrive at.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:08.840
Instead, use the
appropriate mindset shifts

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.450
and the habit-bunching tool

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.840
and whatever other tools
at your disposal you have

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.510
to help you love the process

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.440
and help you love doing these
things for their own sake.

